faqs:
  - q: "What is HubSpot governance?"
    a: "HubSpot governance is the set of rules that keeps a portal understandable and safe as it grows: who can access and change what, how properties and assets are named and owned, how data is validated, and how automation, integrations and reports are reviewed."
  - q: "How often should you review HubSpot governance?"
    a: "Run the full checklist every quarter, after a migration, and before any major rebuild. Weekly, check the fast-moving items: duplicates, workflow errors and sync errors."
  - q: "Who should own HubSpot governance?"
    a: "One named portal owner, usually in operations or RevOps, with property and workflow owners named for each area. If nobody owns the portal, governance decays within months; that is the gap ongoing HubSpot administration fills."
